<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
DESIGN LEDGER: ankle study v2 / locked; 2026-09-11; CONCEPT, UNVERIFIED.
Canonical editable URDF for this isolated concept; not an output of the legacy generator.
SI units; body +X forward, +Y left, +Z up; existing STL files in mm scaled by .001.
Inherited root, hip and knee transforms/meshes: quadruped_robot.urdf and its CAD ledger.
Target consumer: a future separate Isaac Lab ankle-study importer/task, not current V43/V44.
Links: inherited physical links keep their frames; camera_optical_frame is massless.
New foot frames coincide with distal fork axes at distal-local (0.159896689,0,0), RPY zero.
Foot local +X points down at neutral; local Y spans fore/aft, Z spans lateral.
Four fixed ankle_pitch connections at zero; no ankle action channels.
Ankle joints are mechanically locked, not high-gain actuators.
Added servo cases fixed to distal links, pointed toward knee; output drives foot yoke.
Per ankle: 55 g ST3215 + assumed 15 g fixed cradle + 10 g moving yoke.
All feet: sole box 100 x 60 x 6 mm, 1 mm tread, upper face 24 mm below pivot.
Inherited fork-tip spheres removed; contact comes from separate physical foot links.
Servo visual reuses catalog ST3215 mesh; cradle/yoke boxes are packaging concepts, not fitted parts.
Inertials: closed-form box plus parallel-axis arithmetic; assumptions saved in cad/specs/ankle-v2-calculations.json.
Non-servo dry estimate scaled by 0.466834451394; known 55 g servo masses preserved.
Old centered .45 kg pack replaced by separate .523179545 kg rear payload at (-.1315,0,.05).
Total nominal mass 3.50 kg; measured whole mass only constrains baseline total, not COM/inertia distribution.
URDF effort limits on legacy joints reduced to .8825985 Nm for this common conservative study.
URDF alone supplies no torque-speed coupling, latency, friction material, controller or RL task.
No fit sweeps, URDF validation, rendering, simulations, training, hardware or manufacturing checks run.
Collision guards inherited; motor/bracket vs fork fit, foot sweep and bearing/fastener interfaces unresolved.
-->

